audience: Verification owners and reviewers
purpose: Under what conditions and criteria is the effect and cost of adopting the standard judged?

docs/verification/adoption.md is the active verification spec (version 1) for judging the effect and cost of adopting the standard; it separates checker correctness (repeatable experiments) from team time savings (recorded human time) and refuses to read passing tests as productivity.
Translated from Korean in full: scope, test conditions, pass criteria (0 normal-input failures, both injected errors fail under managed, success after restore, paired median delay <= 5 s), the 10-change threshold for team effect, the unchanged-body inconsistency count, required records, and the measurement command.
Headings renamed to Scope / Conditions / Verdict criteria by item / Evidence and execution so the case-sensitive type patterns match.
No Korean literals retained; the command block is unchanged.
Compared against HEAD; no criteria, numbers or conditions dropped. Limitation: self-review by the translator.

